 Here's a Javascript function that should meet your requirements. This function takes an object as its argument, a string `key` representing the dotted path to the desired value, and returns an array containing all entries in the object that have a property with the matching key value:

```javascript
function findEntriesByValue(obj, key) {
  let parts = key.split("."); // Split the key into an array of parts
  let current = obj; // Set the current object to the initial object

  for (let i = 0; i < parts.length; i++) {
    if (!current[parts[i]]) {
      // If the current part doesn't exist, return an empty array
      return [];
    }

    current = current[parts[i]]; // Move to the next level in the object
  }

  // Use Object.values() and filter the results based on the matching value
  let values = Object.values(current);
  let matchingEntries = values.filter((value) => value === current[key]);

  // Return the entries as an array
  return matchingEntries.map((value) => ({
    [key]: value,
  }));
}
```

This function first splits the given key into an array of parts using `String.prototype.split()`. It then iterates through each part in the array, moving from one level of the object to the next until it reaches the final property. Once it has reached the target property, it uses `Object.values()` to get all values at that level, filters out those that don't match the provided key value, and then maps the remaining values back into an object with the original key.

