```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Display User's Desktop Background</title>
    <style>
        body {
            height: 100vh;
            width: 100%;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #EEE; /* Default fallback background color */
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <button onclick="getUserBackgroundColor()">Show Desktop Background Color</button>
    <script>
        function getUserBackgroundColor() {
            var userStyle = document.userStyleSheet || document.styleSheets[0];
            var backgroundColor = userStyle ? userStyle.cssRules[0].style.backgroundColor : 'default';

            if (backgroundColor == 'default') {
                alert('Unable to retrieve the desktop background color.');
            } else {
                document.body.style.backgroundColor = backgroundColor;
                alert('The user\'s desktop background color is: ' + backgroundColor);
            }
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code will show an alert box containing the user's desktop background color when the button is clicked. Note that it only works in some older browsers as most modern ones do not support getting the user's desktop background color via JavaScript due to security reasons.

