 To register a GoDaddy domain with your personal Linux machine without using a VPS, you'll need to set up Dynamic DNS (DDNS) and configure your router to update the IP address of your Linux machine automatically. Here's a step-by-step guide:

1. Set up Dynamic DNS:
   - Sign up for a free DDNS service like `dyn.com`, `no-ip.com`, or any other free provider that supports GoDaddy.
