     ```
     sudo apt-get install ddns2d
     ```
   - Configure the DDNS client by editing the configuration file located at `/etc/ddns2d.conf`. Add the following lines:
     ```
     updateProcedure "myupdate" {
         protocol Txt;
         updateServer "members.dyndns.org";
         updateLogin "your_username";
         updatePassword "your_password";
         updateDomain "your_domain_name.dyndns.org";
     };

     scheduler {
         every 60 minutes;
         updateProcedure "myupdate";
     };
     ```
   - Replace `your_username`, `your_password`, and `your_domain_name` with your actual username, password, and domain name. Save and close the file.
   - Start the DDNS client service:
     ```
     sudo systemctl start ddns2d
     sudo systemctl enable ddns2d
     ```

